    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0510" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg406"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">362.1163 Watch Tower/8: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Berlin (Messersmith) to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-05-02T16:00:00+01:00">May 2, 1933—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 2—11:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to the Department’s telegram No. 46, April 27, 6 p.m., to the Embassy,
                    I am able to report Watch Tower Society premises again free and Society
                    functioning through the good offices of the Consulate General.</p>
                <p>Full report by mail my despatch No. 1269.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d283-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Messersmith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
